          #MixedUnitaryChannelsOnSIngleQBitAreUnistochastic.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              On a single
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/qbit"} qbit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mixed+unitary+quantum+channel"} mixed unitary quantum channel
              is a unistochastic channel.
          (
          %a{:href => "#Müller-HermesPerry19"}> Müller-Hermes &amp; Perry 2019, Cor 1.4
          )
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              By Exp.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniformlyMixedUnitaryChannelsAreUnistochastic"}
              one is reduced to showing that on QBits every mixed unitary quantum channel equals one with uniformly distributed unitaries (this is
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Müller-HermesPerry19"} M-H &amp; P 19, Thm. 1.2
              = succeed "):" do
                %a{:href => "#Müller-HermesPerry19"} M-H &amp; P 19, Lem. 1.1
            %p So let the mixed unitary channel be given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ↦
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msubsup
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                      %mo †
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo +
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msubsup
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                      %mo †
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\rho
                    \\;\mapsto\;
                    p_1 \, U_1 \cdot \rho \cdot U_1^\dagger
                    \\;+\;
                    p_2 \, U_2 \cdot \rho \cdot U_2^\dagger
            %p
              then we want to find
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U'_i
              with
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mtext -
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msubsup
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                      %mo †
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo +
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mtext -
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msubsup
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                      %mo †
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi U
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mtext -
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi U
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ′
                      %mn 1
                      %mo †
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo +
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi U
                    %msub
                      %mo ′
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mtext -
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi U
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ′
                      %mn 2
                      %mo †
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    p_1 \, U_1 \cdot (\text{-}) \cdot U_1^\dagger
                    \\;+\;
                    p_2 \, U_2 \cdot (\text{-}) \cdot U_2^\dagger
                    \\;\;
                    \=
                    \\;\;
                    \\tfrac{1}{2}
                    \\,
                    U'_1 \cdot (\text{-}) \cdot U'_1^\dagger
                    \\;+\;
                    \\tfrac{1}{2}
                    \\,
                    U'_2 \cdot (\text{-}) \cdot U'_2^\dagger
                    \\,.
            %p
              First, by replacing
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mtext -
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mtext -
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mo †
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\text{-}) \mapsto S \cdot (\text{-}) S^\dagger
              — for a unitary
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              to be specified in a moment —, this is equivalent to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mn 1
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi S
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mtext -
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⋅
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mo †
                          %mo ⋅
                          %msubsup
                            %mi U
                            %mn 1
                            %mo †
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mn 2
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi S
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mtext -
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⋅
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mo †
                          %mo ⋅
                          %msubsup
                            %mi U
                            %mn 2
                            %mo †
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mn 2
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi U
                          %msub
                            %mo ′
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi S
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mtext -
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⋅
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mo †
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi U
                          %msubsup
                            %mo ′
                            %mn 1
                            %mo †
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mn 2
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi U
                          %msub
                            %mo ′
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi S
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mtext -
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⋅
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mo †
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi U
                          %msubsup
                            %mo ′
                            %mn 2
                            %mo †
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{r}
                    p_1 \, U_1 \cdot S \cdot (\text{-}) \cdot S^\dagger \cdot U_1^\dagger
                    \\\
                    +\;
                    p_2 \, U_2 \cdot S \cdot (\text{-}) \cdot S^\dagger \cdot U_2^\dagger
                    \\end{array}
                    \\;\;
                    \=
                    \\;\;
                    \\begin{array}{r}
                    \\tfrac{1}{2}
                    \\,
                    U'_1 \cdot S \cdot (\text{-}) \cdot S^\dagger \cdot U'_1^\dagger
                    \\\
                    +
                    \\;
                    \\tfrac{1}{2}
                    \\,
                    U'_2 \cdot S \cdot (\text{-}) \cdot S^\dagger \cdot U'_2^\dagger
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
                    \\end{array}
            %p
              and then conjugating both sides by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mo †
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msubsup
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                      %mo †
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^\dagger \cdot U^\dagger_1
              gives that this is equivalent to
            #eq:IntermediateStepInQBitArgument.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mtext -
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo +
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mo †
                          %msubsup
                            %mi U
                            %mn 1
                            %mo †
                          %mo ⋅
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi S
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mi D
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mtext -
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mo †
                          %mo ⋅
                          %msubsup
                            %mi U
                            %mn 2
                            %mo †
                          %mo ⋅
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mi S
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi D
                          %mo †
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mn 2
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %munder
                            %munder
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mo †
                                %mo ⋅
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi U
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mo †
                                %mo ⋅
                                %mi U
                                %msub
                                  %mo ′
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ⋅
                                %mi S
                              %mo ⏟
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi W
                                %mn 1
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mtext -
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⋅
                          %munder
                            %munder
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mo †
                                %mo ⋅
                                %mi U
                                %msubsup
                                  %mo ′
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mo †
                                %mo ⋅
                                %msub
                                  %mi U
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ⋅
                                %mi S
                              %mo ⏟
                            %mrow
                              %msubsup
                                %mi W
                                %mn 1
                                %mo †
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                            %mfrac
                              %mn 1
                              %mn 2
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %munder
                            %munder
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mo †
                                %mo ⋅
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi U
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mo †
                                %mo ⋅
                                %mi U
                                %msub
                                  %mo ′
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo ⋅
                                %mi S
                              %mo ⏟
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi W
                                %mn 2
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mtext -
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⋅
                          %munder
                            %munder
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi S
                                  %mo †
                                %mo ⋅
                                %mi U
                                %msubsup
                                  %mo ′
                                  %mn 2
                                  %mo †
                                %mo ⋅
                                %msub
                                  %mi U
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ⋅
                                %mi S
                              %mo ⏟
                            %mrow
                              %msubsup
                                %mi W
                                %mn 2
                                %mo †
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    p_1 \, (\text{-})
                    \\;+\;
                    p_2 \,
                    \\underset{D}{
                    \\underbrace{
                    S^\dagger U_1^\dagger \cdot U_2 \cdot S
                    } }
                    \\cdot
                    (\text{-})
                    \\cdot
                    \\underset{D^\dagger}{
                    \\underbrace{
                    S^\dagger \cdot U_2^\dagger \cdot U_1 \cdot S
                    }
                    }
                    \\;\;
                    \=
                    \\;\;
                    \\begin{array}{r}
                    \\tfrac{1}{2}
                    \\,
                    \\underset{ W_1 }{
                    \\underbrace{
                    S^\dagger \cdot U_1^\dagger \cdot U'_1 \cdot S
                    }
                    }
                    \\cdot
                    (\text{-})
                    \\cdot
                    \\underset{
                    W_1^\dagger
                    }{
                    \\underbrace{
                    S^\dagger \cdot U'_1^\dagger \cdot U_1 \cdot S
                    }
                    }
                    \\\
                    +
                    \\;
                    \\tfrac{1}{2}
                    \\,
                    \\underset{
                    W_2
                    }{
                    \\underbrace{
                    S^\dagger \cdot U_1^\dagger \cdot U'_2 \cdot S
                    }
                    }
                    \\cdot
                    (\text{-})
                    \\cdot
                    \\underset{W_2^\dagger}{
                    \\underbrace{
                    S^\dagger \cdot U'_2^\dagger \cdot U_1 \cdot S
                    }
                    }
                    \\end{array}
            %p
              At this point we fix
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                      %mo †
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1^\dagger \cdot U_2
              is evidently a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+operator"} normal operator
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+theorem"} spectral theorem
              applies to show that we may find
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              above is a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+matrix"} diagonal matrix
            #eq:DiagonalizingOperatorInQBitArgument.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msubsup
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                      %mo †
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mo †
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi diag
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 11
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 22
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi D
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S \cdot U_1^\dagger \cdot U_2 \cdot S^\dagger
                    \\;\;=\;\;
                    diag\big( D_{11}, \, D_{22} \big)
                    \\,=\,
                    D
                    \\,.
            %p
              This way we are now reduced to finding unitary operators
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_i
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mtext -
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo +
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi D
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mtext -
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mo †
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mtext -
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msubsup
                      %mi W
                      %mn 1
                      %mo †
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo +
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mtext -
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msubsup
                      %mi W
                      %mn 2
                      %mo †
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    p_1 \, (\text{-})
                    \\;+\;
                    p_2
                    \\,
                    D \cdot (\text{-}) \cdot D^\dagger
                    \\;\;
                    \=
                    \\;\;
                    \\tfrac{1}{2}
                    \\,
                    W_1 \cdot (\text{-}) \cdot W_1^\dagger
                    \\;+\;
                    \\tfrac{1}{2}
                    \\,
                    W_2 \cdot (\text{-}) \cdot W_2^\dagger
                    \\,.
            %p Plugging in the simple ansatz
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %mn 2
                                  %mi π
                                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} i
                                  %msub
                                    %mi ϕ
                                    %mi i
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mn 1
                      %mo ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    W_i
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left[
                    \\array{
                    e^{2 \pi \mathrm{i} \phi_i } &amp; 0
                    \\\
                    0 &amp; 1
                    }
                    \\right]
            %p shows that this works for
            #eq:PhaseConditionForQBitArgument.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi π
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} i
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi π
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} i
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mn 2
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo +
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 11
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mn 22
                      %mo ¯
                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tfrac{1}{2}
                    \\big(
                    e^{2 \pi \mathrm{i} \phi_1}
                    +
                    e^{2 \pi \mathrm{i} \phi_2}
                    \\big)
                    \\;\;
                    \=
                    \\;\;
                    p_1
                    \\,+\,
                    p_2
                    \\,
                    D_11 \overline{D_22}
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
            %p
              which always has a solution for the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_i
              (
