                    \\begin{array}{rcl}
                    flip_p(\rho)
                    \&amp;=&amp;
                    \\tfrac{1}{2}
                    \\,
                    \\left[
                    \\array{
                    cos(\phi/2) &amp; -\mathrm{i}\,sin(\phi/2)
                    \\\
                    \-\mathrm{i}\,sin(\phi/2) &amp; cos(\phi/2)
                    }
                    \\right]
                    \\cdot
                    \\rho
                    \\cdot
                    \\left[
                    \\array{
                    cos(\phi/2) &amp; +\mathrm{i}\,sin(\phi/2)
                    \\\
                    +\mathrm{i}\,sin(\phi/2) &amp; cos(\phi/2)
                    }
                    \\right]
                    \\\
                    \&amp;+&amp;
                    \\tfrac{1}{2}
                    \\,
                    \\left[
                    \\array{
                    cos(\phi/2) &amp; +\mathrm{i}\,sin(\phi/2)
                    \\\
                    +\mathrm{i}\,sin(\phi/2) &amp; cos(\phi/2)
                    }
                    \\right]
                    \\cdot
                    \\rho
                    \\cdot
                    \\left[
                    \\array{
                    cos(\phi/2) &amp; -\mathrm{i}\,sin(\phi/2)
                    \\\
                    \-\mathrm{i}\,sin(\phi/2) &amp; cos(\phi/2)
                    }
                    \\right]
                    \\mathrlap{\,,}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\text{where}\;
                    \\phi
                    \\,\equiv\,
                    arccos(1-2p)
                    \\text{.}
                    \\end{array}
            %p
              With
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CouplingMatrixForUniformMixedUnitaryChannel"} (1)
              this uniformly mixed unitary presentation immediately gives the unistochastic presentation of the bit-flip channel.
          %h2#references References
          %h3#dqc1_computation DQC1 computation
          %p
            The exploration of the possibilities of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+computing"} quantum computing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+information+theory"} quantum information theory
            with (a few or even just single) “clean”
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/qubits"} qubits
            coupled to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximally+mixed+state"} maximally mixed state
            environment goes back to
          %ul
            %li#KnillLaflamme98
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emanuel+Knill"}> Emanuel Knill
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Raymond+Laflamme"} Raymond Laflamme
              = succeed "," do
                %em On the Power of One Bit of Quantum Information
              %strong 81
              (1998) 5672-5675 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/9802037"}> arXiv:quant-ph/9802037
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.81.5672"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.81.5672
          %p
            (motivated by the practical reality of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NMR"} NMR
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+resonance+qbits"} spin resonance qbits
            = succeed "." do
              %em deterministic quantum computation with one quantum bit (DQC1)
          %p The model was further discussed in:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Poulin"}> David Poulin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Raymond+Laflamme"} Raymond Laflamme
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gerard+J.+Milburn"} Gerard J. Milburn
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Juan+Pablo+Paz"} Juan Pablo Paz
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Testing integrability with a single bit of quantum information
                %strong 68
                22302 (2003) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0303042"}> arXiv:quant-ph/0303042
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevA.68.022302"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevA.68.022302
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Poulin"}> David Poulin
                , Robin Blume-Kohout,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Raymond+Laflamme"} Raymond Laflamme
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Exponential speed-up with a single bit of quantum information: Testing the quantum butterfly effect
                %strong 92
                177906 (2004) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0310038"}> arXiv:quant-ph/0310038
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.92.177906"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.92.177906
            %li#Shor08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+W.+Shor"}> Peter W. Shor
                , Stephen P. Jordan,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Estimating Jones polynomials is a complete problem for one clean qubit
                %strong 8
                (2008) 681 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0707.2831"}> arXiv:0707.2831
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.5555/2017011.2017012"} doi:10.5555/2017011.2017012
            %li
              %p
                Dan Shepherd,
                %em Computation with Unitaries and One Pure Qubit
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0608132"}> arXiv:quant-ph/0608132
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Chris Cade, Ashley Montanaro,
                %em
                  The Quantum Complexity of Computing Schatten
                  = succeed "-norms" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.09279"}> arXiv:1706.09279
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One_Clean_Qubit"} One Clean QBit
          %p Discussion where even the single system qbit is not fully coherent, either:
          %ul
            %li
              Tomoyuki Morimae, Keisuke Fujii, Harumichi Nishimura,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Power of one non-clean qubit
              %em 95
              042336 (2017) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.07244"}> arXiv:1610.07244
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevA.95.042336"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevA.95.042336
          %p
            Proof that all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unital+quantum+channels"} unital quantum channels
            on single
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/qubits"} qubits
            are unistochastic (noisy operations) for a bath of size at least 4:
          %ul
            %li{:id => "Müller-HermesPerry19"}
              Alexander Müller-Hermes, Christopher Perry,
              = succeed "," do
                %em All unital qubit channels are 4-noisy operations
              %strong 109
              (2019) 1–9 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s11005-018-1104-x"}> doi:10.1007/s11005-018-1104-x
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.01337"} arXiv:1802.01337
          %p
            Discussion of DQC1 in the language of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+channels"} quantum channels
          %ul
            %li#XuerebCampbellGooldXuereb23
              %p
                Jake Xuereb, Steve Campbell, John Goold, André Xuereb,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em DQC1 as an Open Quantum System
                %strong 107
                042222 (2023) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.03947"}> arXiv:2209.03947
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevA.107.042222"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevA.107.042222
            %li#FuHeLiLuo23
              %p
                Shuangshuang Fu, Jiayu He, Xiaohui Li and Shunlong Luo,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Uncertainties and coherence in DQC1
                %strong 98
                4 (2023) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1088/1402-4896/acc5ba"}> doi:10.1088/1402-4896/acc5ba
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Discussion of classical simulation (or not) of the DQC1 model
          %ul
            %li#FKMNTT18
              Keisuke Fujii, Hirotada Kobayashi, Tomoyuki Morimae, Harumichi Nishimura, Shuhei Tamate, Seiichiro Tani,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Impossibility of Classically Simulating One-Clean-Qubit Computation
              %strong 120
              200502 (2018) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1409.6777"}> arXiv:1409.6777
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.120.200502"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.120.200502
          %h3#noisy_operationsunistochastic_channels Noisy operations/unistochastic channels
          %p The terminology of “noisy operations” is due to
          %ul
            %li#HorodeckiHorodeckiOppenheim03
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michal+Horodecki"}> Michal Horodecki
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pawel+Horodecki"} Pawel Horodecki
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Oppenheim"} Jonathan Oppenheim
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Reversible transformations from pure to mixed states, and the unique measure of information
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevA.67.062104"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevA.67.062104
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0212019"} arXiv;quant-ph/0212019
            %li
              %p
                picked up by
                %a{:href => "#Müller-HermesPerry19"} Müller-Hermes &amp; Perry 2019
          %p and the terminology “unistochastic channels” was introduced in:
          %ul
            %li{:id => "ŻyczkowskiBengtsson04"}
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karol+%C5%BByczkowski"}> Karol Życzkowski
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ingemar+Bengtsson"} Ingemar Bengtsson
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On Duality between Quantum Maps and Quantum States
                %strong 11
                01 (2004) 3-42 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1023/B:OPSY.0000024753.05661.c2"}> doi:10.1023/B:OPSY.0000024753.05661.c2
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li{:id => "BengtssonŻyczkowski06"}
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ingemar+Bengtsson"}> Ingemar Bengtsson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karol+%C5%BByczkowski"} Karol Życzkowski
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometry of Quantum States — An Introduction to Quantum Entanglement
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511535048"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511535048
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/266435541_Geometry_of_Quantum_States_An_Introduction_to_Quantum_Entanglement"} ResearchGate
            %li
              %p
                Marcin Musz, Marek Kuś,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karol+%C5%BByczkowski"} Karol Życzkowski
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Unitary quantum gates, perfect entanglers, and unistochastic maps
                %strong 87
                (2013) 022111 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevA.87.022111"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevA.87.022111
                \&amp;rbrack;
